# The Dockerfile's build stage does `COPY . .`, so without this file the build
# context is the whole working tree — including .env with the live Gemini key,
# data/quotes.db with 225 real customers, and 208 MB of node_modules that are
# about to be rebuilt anyway. Everything listed here is either a secret, state
# that must come from a volume, or dead weight.

# Secrets. The image is pushed to a registry and pulled onto other machines;
# nothing here may carry a credential.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# State. data/ is the SQLite database and belongs to a volume, not a layer —
# baking it in would ship one machine's quotations to every other machine and
# then lose them on the next redeploy.
data/
.tmp/
.preview/

# Rebuilt inside the image. node_modules is linux-native after `npm ci`; a
# Windows copy would break better-sqlite3's native addon.
node_modules/
web/dist/
dist/

# History and tooling the runtime never reads.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
*.log

# Reference documents the desk supplied, not loaded by the application.
Supporting Documents/

# Windows and editor droppings.
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
~$*
.vscode/
.idea/

# NOT ignored, and deliberately so — the test stage runs the real suite:
#   Resources/                      importCustomers.test.ts reads it (33 tests)
#   Quotation -- Format.docx        docx.test.ts, build-template.ts
#   Quotation-Morgan Stanley*.docx  docx.test.ts
#   Quotation-DGSL*.docx            parser.test.ts, render-preview.ts
# Excluding any of them makes those tests fail or silently skip in CI.
